response-og: ```python
def act(state):
    """
    Deterministic policy for the MountainCar environment.

    - If the car is moving left (velocity < 0) keep accelerating left.
    - If it is moving right (velocity > 0) keep accelerating right.
    - When velocity is exactly zero we need a tie‑breaker:
        • Near the start of an episode (position ≈ -0.5) we should
          continue left so the car can build momentum.
        • At the leftmost bound of the valley (position ≤ -0.9) we
          must switch to right to avoid getting stuck at the wall.
    """
    pos, vel = state

    if vel < 0:
        # Car is moving left – keep pushing left.
        return 0
    elif vel > 0:
        # Car is moving right – push right towards the goal.
        return 2
    else:  # vel == 0
        # Zero velocity: decide based on position.
        # At the start (around -0.5) go left; at the left wall go right.
        if pos < -0.9:
            return 2  # avoid being stuck at the left bound
        else:
            return 0
```
